{
  "id": "simulation-over-a-machine",
  "goals": [
    "LeanExe.A64.Machine P code α for a model with more state than the program's, such as a process with FPCR and a trace",
    "M.lift : M.SR cap gts st q → Reach P code (M.core q) s → ∃ q', M.Rch q q' ∧ M.core q' = s ∧ ...",
    "a store relation SR that adds a fact to StoreRel, which every run of the program's model must keep",
    "M.Trapped S st msg q for an exit whose store holds the status and the world",
    "Outcome P code ... = (bare P code α).Outcome ... by rfl",
    "InstrSim P code F inst from ∀ α, (bare P code α).InstrSim F inst",
    "M.InstrSim F inst for a form that neither calls nor reads the host",
    "LeanExe.A64.Leaf inst",
    "M.FunSim m S need g k (entry, imp.params, imp.results) for an import whose code is a stub",
    "M.CallsOk F m callee S need for a table of stubs and generated functions",
    "a run relation of a process whose steps require FPCR or a bound on the program counter",
    "LeanExe.A64.withMachine T R P Pp hP code hdom hk hk18 area gap H K hK Ex env",
    "a fact about memory outside the area that every run of the module's code keeps",
    "LeanExe.A64.Platform.Le P Pp with a relation K on the memory outside P's Normal memory",
    "a stub that writes between the area's end and the stack's limit, against the frame from SP up",
    "t.x 17 = s.x 17 or t.x 18 = s.x 18 for every run of the module's code",
    "M.StubSim S n ps rs hf entry for a stub that reads the scratch or Linux's initial stack",
    "a loop of A64 code over a zero-terminated string or a vector of pointers",
    "∀ q, KeptReg q → u.x q = s.x q from the frame lemmas of a run's segments"
  ],
  "modules": [
